From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:26:11 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-neocd

Neo Geo CD discs get their own shelf, Games/NEOCD, for .cue and .chd,
on NeoCD (neocd_libretro) alone: Platform::Neocd after SegaCd,
Core::Neocd after MednafenSupergrafx. Track files and playlists stay
off the shelf, and a disc on the Neo Geo shelf is skipped there. It
plays like the Neo Geo shelf: A, B, C and D on B, A, Y and X, SELECT
and START to the game, L1 and R1 to the game, L2 and R2 kept by slot,
and the picture toggle on SELECT+X.

NeoCD is told the CDZ BIOS (neocd.bin, the fastest loader), the USA
region (the English text of a dual-language disc), its CD speed hack
and load skip on, a 1:1 picture (slot draws the aspect) and no
overclock. Its own backup RAM file is one shared neocd.srm named before
the options are read, so slot keeps each game's 8 KB backup RAM in
Saves/NEOCD/<stem>.sav and hands a game without one a blank backup RAM
rather than another game's. A state is about 8 MB, so rewind is off
like the PlayStation; save states, resume, fast-forward and the crash
guard work as on every shelf.

The Screen page gains a Neo Geo CD section, last: Shader (the retro
list, Config/neocd_shader.txt) and Picture, Stretch by default then
Actual and 4:3, kept in Config/picture.txt as neocd. The release date
for the shelf order is 9 September 1994, between CPS2 and the 32X. A
disc wears the jewel case, the Japanese one with its spine strip for a
disc tagged (Japan).
